WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:06.270
Wednesday Season 2 is shaping up to be huge,
with a big mystery about who's behind those

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.940
threatening messages, the possible return
of Miss Thornhill and Principal Weems, and

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.380
perhaps a secret new master controlling the
Hyde.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.410
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'll be explaining everything you

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.220
can look forward to in the second season of
Wednesday.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.580
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.410
Laurel, aka Miss Thornhill, the evil mastermind
behind everything in Season 1, ends up in

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.670
a really bad way by the final episode, covered
in bees and with Wednesday's boot coming down

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.610
to stomp her in the face.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.969
Many people have assumed this means the villainous
school teacher is dead, but I don't think

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:45.559
that's the case and I'm pretty certain Netflix
will want to bring Christina Ricci back to

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:46.559
the show.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:51.420
There's also the fact we never see what happens
to her body after Wednesday's stomp, and a

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.310
great comment by movie lover "Mojolytical"
points out that Crackstone's ring will probably

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.690
have something to do with Laurel's return.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:03.140
As the evil resurrected pilgrim burned up,
the ring on his finger fell to the ground,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:08.060
and there was a deliberate slow-motion close-up
shot of the ring, a signal that it will surely

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.110
play a part in the future.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.930
At the end, she was also lying on the ground
not far from where Crackstone's ring fell,

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:20.270
so if we assume she survived and crawled off,
she could have easily spotted the ring, taking

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.270
it with her.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.110
The ring features a kraken – a legendary
sea monster – wrapping its tentacles around

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.110
a ship.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:31.110
This feels like a hint that the villainous
Laurel and Tyler are part of an even bigger

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:35.990
monstrous plot directed at Wednesday and perhaps
the entire Addams family.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.080
Were Laurel Gates and Tyler just pawns in
a bigger game?

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:43.680
A character who appeared to be a lot more
dead by the end of Season 1 was Principal

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.950
Weems, who was injected with deadly Nightshade
poison by Laurel after she and Wednesday confronted

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:49.950
her.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.640
Now, tons of you have said you really aren't
ready for Larissa Weems to be gone, and I

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.960
do think there's a decent possibility that
Weems secretly survived.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.740
Given Weems and Wednesday knew about Laurel's
predilection for chemical manipulation, Weems

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.810
might have consumed an antidote earlier to
counteract the poison.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.690
Weems is also a shapeshifter, so it's possible
she cast an illusion to show herself dying,

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.810
but in reality she was OK.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:19.100
Now, I'm not saying that Weems is alive for
sure, as it can cheapen a character's sacrifice

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.590
if a death is too easily reversed in a movie
or TV show.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:27.250
However, we never saw a funeral for Weems
like we did with the dead mayor, and Gwendoline

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.740
Christie said the following in an interview
about Season 2:

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:33.250
"We haven't seen her put in the ground, have
we?

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.860
I feel like Larissa Weems would not really
be prepared to entertain or be dominated by

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.599
anything as commonplace as death."

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:44.910
The last few moments of the finale leave us
with a big question about who could be behind

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.820
the threatening messages on Wednesday's new
phone.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.400
Although I expect Laurel to be returning,
I doubt it's her, but it is likely to be the

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.430
main villain for Season 2, so let's run through
the likeliest candidates.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:02.650
A great comment by movie lover "Fabula Sumus"
says it will turn out to be Xavier's father,

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.260
a character we haven't yet met, but who was
mentioned multiple times in Season 1.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.409
My dad's a psychic.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:09.409
Vincent Thorpe.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:10.849
My brother's his number one fan.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:14.800
Watched his Vegas Special so many times, I'm
surprised it's not imprinted on his eyeballs.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.590
Xavier's dad appears to be quite a cold character
and uninterested in his son.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.650
He didn't show up on Parents' Weekend or when
he was arrested, and he's uncaring about some

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:28.180
of the difficulties Xavier experiences with
his powers.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.340
My father thinks that my mental health is
a PR problem that he needs to manage.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.239
Vincent could have some dark secrets from
his former time at Nevermore that he'd prefer

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:38.239
were kept quiet.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:43.150
So if he discovered Wednesday has been snooping
around, he might have decided to scare her

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.430
off further investigations.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:50.689
As Xavier's dad, it wouldn't be too difficult
for him to access his son's phone to get Wednesday's

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:53.430
number and send her the threatening texts.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.849
Thanks to his fame, he might be recruited
as the new principal to replace Weems.

00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:01.580
And given that Xavier's family already met
the Addams family in the past...

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.099
It was my godmother's funeral.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:04.549
Apparently she was friends with your grandmother.

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:09.549
...it'd be interesting to see how he interacts
with Morticia and Gomez if they cross paths

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.549
again.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:15.290
A suspicious character we haven't met yet
is Gideon, the MorningSong cult leader mentioned

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.410
by Gabrielle, Bianca's mum.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:18.840
Gideon said you'd resist.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.280
You think he'd give a damn about some single
mom and her daughter if we weren't sirens?

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.410
I think the cult may have designs on Jericho
and its inhabitants.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:31.570
For example, we saw how Bianca's mother convinced
Lucas to download the cult's self-help app

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.990
just in the weekend she came to visit.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:38.531
Although Bianca later persuaded him to ditch
it, I think MorningSong may try to recruit

00:04:38.531 --> 00:04:43.270
more normies from the town and perhaps even
Nevermore students who, with their powers

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:47.160
and abilities, could be a way of boosting
the cult and its influence.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.440
They may already have some nefarious, secret
activities they're engaged in at the Academy

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.840
or in the town and might be trying to scare
off Wednesday from snooping around any further

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.440
with the threatening messages.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:03.630
A possible character we have met who could
be the stalker is Yoko the vampire, as many

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.060
of you've pointed out.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:10.870
Indeed, Yoko was namedropped quite a few times,
but didn't get many lines, so I think she

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.080
and perhaps the vampires as a whole might
get more focus in the second season.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.090
But why would Yoko hold a grudge against Wednesday?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:24.370
Well, a smallish reason might be how Enid
went to room-share with Yoko after she fell

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.030
out with Wednesday, and they really seemed
to hit it off.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:30.210
Yoko and I are so in sync that she's begging
me to be her new roomie.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:33.630
But later Enid dumped Yoko to room again with
Wednesday.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.910
A more significant reason though might be
that Yoko has some history with Wednesday's

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:42.370
mother Morticia, as apparently many of the
vampires at Nevermore have been there for

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.130
a very long time.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:45.919
Those are the Fangs, AKA vampires.

00:05:45.919 --> 00:05:48.750
Some of them have literally been here for
decades.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:52.970
The sheriff is another existing character
with reasons to dislike Wednesday.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:57.380
He was already suspicious of her in the first
episode because of his history with her family.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.900
I'm gonna keep my eye on you.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:02.990
He might also resent her for exposing his
son Tyler as a Hyde;

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:07.970
and given his job, he could probably find
out her number to send her the messages.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:13.020
Another possibility is Kent, the Siren guy
who was thumped in the face by Thing and about

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.930
whom Wednesday didn't hide what she thought
in front of the other Nightshades when she

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.550
explained how she'd discovered their secret
meeting room.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.940
I thought we just snapped twice.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.680
Well, aren't you the brightest in the bunch?

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.190
There's also Lucas.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:28.639
Although he turned good by the end thanks
to Bianca, he and his mates have an antagonistic

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:32.970
history with Wednesday and she fought them
after they harassed her at the coffee shop.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:37.599
It's a long shot, but another possibility
is that Wednesday's stalker is the jock from

00:06:37.599 --> 00:06:41.000
her former high school who bullied her brother
Pugsley.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.430
He might have tracked her down in Jericho
and is looking for revenge for the piranhas

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:46.729
in the swimming pool.

00:06:46.729 --> 00:06:51.130
The showrunners have already confirmed that
although the series is focused around Wednesday,

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.370
they do plan to bring back the rest of the
Addams Family in Season 2.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:07:00.210
Some fun ideas are that Pugsley could attend
Nevermore and Morticia could even take over

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.700
as principal for the missing Weems.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.840
Given the former principal's animosity to
Morticia, this could be really interesting

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.950
especially if Weems turns out to be still
alive.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.690
Uncle Fester will surely be back too, and
there were many teases for another Cousin

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:19.510
Itt making an appearance next season, via
the portraits of Ignatius Itt in the basement

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.280
of the Nightshade Society.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:26.330
But just before Wednesday returns to Nevermore,
could we also get some time where she goes

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:28.490
to see Enid in San Francisco?

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.130
I can pretty much guarantee fog and drizzle
every day.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.130
Sounds tempting.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:37.730
The very final shot of the season sees a chained-up
Tyler being taken away, but then Hyding out

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:39.470
into his monster form.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:43.710
An interesting detail that another of our
movie lovers points out here is that Tyler

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:48.949
hyding out happens just as Wednesday's car
is passing the truck transporting his, which

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:51.560
could suggest Wednesday is his new master.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:56.490
If it were the case the best explanation I
can think of is that Wednesday locking him

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.930
up and torturing him, inflicted a trauma that
somehow bonded him to her.

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.970
Born of mutation, the Hyde lays dormant until
unleashed by a traumatic event.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:09.990
I think for Tyler's Season 2 arc he may seek
out his mother, who was never explicitly confirmed

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:10.990
to be dead.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:15.629
She was however locked up as a Hyde and perhaps
he'll find her if he's being taken to the

00:08:15.629 --> 00:08:20.790
same facility, and I think there could be
a possible redemption storyline for him there.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:24.830
And if you want to discover all the amazing
details and easter eggs you might have missed

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:30.170
in Wednesday, like the many inspirations for
Jenna Ortega's Rave'N dance, tap here to watch

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.449
my video on that.

00:08:31.449 --> 00:08:33.240
There's also a link in the video description.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:38.240
So, what are your predictions or what would
you like to see happen in a second season

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.370
of Wednesday?

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.349
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:45.320
And if you enjoyed this video do leave a thumbs-up,
I really appreciate it.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:49.500
Thanks for enjoying Wednesday with me and
hope you have a marvellous movie-loving week!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.910
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

